terms.shortDefinition:
A `[[Texture2D]]` resource that crops a single rectangular `region` (`Rect2`) out of a larger downloaded **Sprite Sheet** (`res://assets/cards/deck_sheet.png`).

Instead of 54 separate image files, many itch.io and Kenney asset packs distribute one combined grid image. `AtlasTexture` lets each `CardData` slice its exact `[suit_row, rank_col]` rectangle at runtime:

```gdscript
const SHEET := preload("res://assets/cards/deck_sheet.png")
func slice_card(col: int, row: int, w: int = 140, h: int = 190) -> AtlasTexture:
    var atlas := AtlasTexture.new()
    atlas.atlas = SHEET
    atlas.region = Rect2(col * w, row * h, w, h)
    return atlas
```
